WEBVTT

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:08.500
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
ima wa ugokenai sore ga sadame dakedo

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
Right now I can't move... That is my fate, but...

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
akirame wa shinai mou mezameta kara

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
I won't give up anymore because I have awakened.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
moeru tokimeki wa jidai wo utsushi

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
My burning, throbbing heart reflects the era...

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
iro azayaka ni moesakaru honoo

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
It has the color of vividly blazing flames...

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying ima wa mienaku tomo

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying, though I can't see it right now...

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching michi shirube wa ukabu

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching, a guidepost floats up ahead.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.170
I wanna have a pure time!

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:48.280
Everyone's a noble mind!

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
soko ni nokotta wakasa toridashi

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
I'll take out what remains of my youth there,

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.980
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.540
beyond the hard times from now!

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
kawaku kuchibiru nureteiru nara

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
If these dry lips become wet,

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
toki wo norikoe atsui jidai e to

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
Beyond time, towards a passionate era,

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
utsuru darou to shinjiteiru kara

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
Because I believe it will move...

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.060
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:23.690
beyond the hard times from now...

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:36.400
What was waiting for Kamille
in outer space were Gabthleys...

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:38.070
...a new mobile suit model.

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:43.950
The Gundam Mk. II was nearly
defeated by the pilots Jerid and Mouar.

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:49.580
Right at that moment, Fa Yuiry arrived
with the A.E.U.G.'s new mobile suit.

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:55.120
The Eyes of Scirocco

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:14.440
I'm prepared to be reproached
for my impertinence.

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:17.970
I lost one of our new mobile suits,
which is inexcusable.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:21.350
That's not why I called you here.

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:24.320
On the contrary, I wanted to tell you
not to feel down about what happened.

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:25.980
Are you sympathizing?

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:27.950
You misunderstand.

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:31.120
In fact, you could say I envy you.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:34.460
It's true that you likely
would've won the battle...

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:37.090
...if it weren't for that
new mobile armor, Lieutenant.

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:39.160
You're very lucky.

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:43.800
The question is,
do you believe in your good luck?

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:45.570
So, you're saying I lack resolve?

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:46.870
That's right.

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:48.500
Keep that in mind.

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:53.510
I'm going to have you lead a battle squadron.

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:56.510
I'll introduce you to your pilots.

00:02:56.590 --> 00:02:58.560
You've seen them around.

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:03.360
<i>Scirocco's bringing Jerid under his wing.</i>

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:06.900
<i>Will Jerid see this as a chance</i>
<i>to grow independent?</i>

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:31.050
Kamille! Well? Like it?!

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:32.550
Yeah, I guess.

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:34.390
Couldn't you sound a little more excited?

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:38.120
The Zeta Gundam's more or less
been built for you, you know!

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:39.920
I know that.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.660
Lieutenant Quattro rushed it over here...

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:43.530
...because he wanted
to show it to you right away!

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:44.430
Lieutenant Quattro did?

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:45.560
Kamille!

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:49.210
Haro!

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:53.740
Kamille! Hello!

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:02.680
Wait, Fa!

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:04.520
But it's Haro you called for, right?

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:05.890
Come on.

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:07.860
You wanted to see me, didn't you?

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:09.860
I came to see the mobile suits.

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:11.830
I wanted to know which one
I'm going to pilot.

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:14.660
Is it true you're a candidate
to be a pilot?

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:18.500
We find ourselves in a grave situation
with the presence of the Titans all around.

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:21.600
We won't get anywhere if we
depend on you all the time, Kamille.

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:26.140
I was hoping that you'd remain in a world
that had nothing to do with wars.

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:31.740
Your opinions are out of touch
with the times.

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:34.150
What if every one of us
is fighting a war?

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:36.480
What happens if we all end up dead?

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:39.320
That's something the victors
can figure out later!

00:04:39.390 --> 00:04:40.760
That's absurd.

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:44.560
In order to win the war, the A.E.U.G.
will send over the Mk. II's Defenser...

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:46.330
...and also a new model mobile suit.

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:48.600
Another new mobile suit,
so soon?

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:51.540
The A.E.U.G.'s build-up on the Moon
has been progressing.

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:53.630
Why don't you face harsh
reality for a change?!

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:56.140
All right, then!

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:11.050
Captain Henken.

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:13.220
I shall be on my way.

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:14.950
Which are you happier about?

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:17.890
Being able to pilot the Methuss,
or returning to the Argama?

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:21.000
Easy, I'm happy about both!

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:22.560
- Ensign Reccoa!
- Yes, sir!

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:26.370
I'd like you to hand this
to Lieutenant Emma!

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:30.200
Take it!

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:31.370
Yes, sir!

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:34.780
Tell them that I'll be heading
for the Argama on the Radish!

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:35.570
Roger!

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:39.350
These are the estimated courses
from Gryps.

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:42.550
The possible courses taken
by the Titans' fleet that left Gryps?

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:43.850
Yes, sir!

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:46.860
Given the timing, their plan must
be to head for the Moon.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:49.730
Tell the observation team to watch
enemy movements closely!

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:51.090
Yes, sir!

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:54.130
Haro, what's wrong?

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:56.990
Kamille and Fa! Fighting!

00:05:57.070 --> 00:05:59.590
My! So soon after they meet?

00:06:00.170 --> 00:06:00.800
Haro!

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:02.700
Kamille! Fa! Cut it out!

00:06:02.770 --> 00:06:04.670
I've already stopped!

00:06:04.810 --> 00:06:07.040
He's always nagging me. Totally unmanly!

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:11.780
Quarrels between pilots will affect
their abilities in battle!

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:13.680
Continue this, and I'll lock you up!

00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:14.510
Yes, sir!

00:06:14.590 --> 00:06:16.550
I'll learn to be more careful!

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:18.110
Just say it won't happen again.

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:19.620
Let them be.

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:22.180
To them, that's just a form of recreation.
Recreation!

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:24.530
Wait!

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:26.220
Let go of me!

00:06:29.170 --> 00:06:30.100
You see...!

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:38.710
What is it?!

00:06:39.510 --> 00:06:40.710
S-Sorry.

00:06:41.010 --> 00:06:44.570
You have nothing to say, right?!
Then go away!

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:47.720
Fa!

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:53.390
There's something odd about you!

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:55.150
Even right now.

00:06:55.230 --> 00:06:57.420
Kamille, your body may have returned
to the Argama...

00:06:57.500 --> 00:06:59.460
...but your heart isn't here with you.

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:06.760
Would you have a word with Kamille,
Lieutenant?

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:09.310
Maybe somebody else
should talk to him.

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:11.870
Why? Can't we just write this off
as his recreation?

00:07:11.940 --> 00:07:13.140
No, we can't.

00:07:13.210 --> 00:07:15.740
Right now, Kamille has the eyes
of a wanderer.

00:07:16.050 --> 00:07:18.020
I'd just make things worse.

00:07:18.350 --> 00:07:19.410
Why's that?

00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:21.710
Kamille is instinctively attracted to me.

00:07:23.590 --> 00:07:25.450
Y-You think so?

00:07:26.930 --> 00:07:29.220
I'm not saying this out of self-conceit.

00:07:29.630 --> 00:07:34.190
Simply put, I don't want to promote
any mother complex Kamille has.

00:07:34.270 --> 00:07:35.260
Really?

00:07:35.330 --> 00:07:38.630
I cannot be a substitute mother for Kamille.

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:41.160
That's a problem.

00:07:41.240 --> 00:07:45.200
There's no choice but to leave Kamille
alone, and wait for him to awaken.

00:07:45.610 --> 00:07:46.580
Phew!

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:49.050
He's as big as a grown adult.

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:50.710
Yet such a problematic kid.

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:55.310
In the Forces, it's the father figure's
job to raise the soldiers, right?

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:56.810
I got you.

00:07:57.360 --> 00:07:58.120
Damn...!

00:07:58.820 --> 00:08:02.090
I didn't expect that I'd be ordered
to baby-sit little children like you.

00:08:02.630 --> 00:08:06.790
For your information, Lieutenant,
I've had sufficient training.

00:08:06.870 --> 00:08:08.800
I'm very disappointed to hear
such a comment from you!

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:13.000
You two are Newtype candidates
selected by Scirocco.

00:08:13.370 --> 00:08:16.810
But look at your hands.

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:18.930
Probably never hurt a soul in your life.

00:08:19.010 --> 00:08:20.480
Are you really prepared to kill?

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:23.510
I will never kill!

00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:26.420
Then what are you a mobile suit pilot for?!

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:31.580
War is an evil but necessary step on
the path to a better world.

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:33.250
We're only fighting for that reason.

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:37.350
Even when engaged in battle, I will
not kill an enemy that I do not have to.

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:40.760
But then the enemy will kill you!

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:42.730
I am not prepared to die yet.

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:44.390
Then why did you become a pilot?!

00:08:46.810 --> 00:08:50.040
I thought private matters
are not questioned in the Forces!

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:53.230
Forget it, then!

00:08:53.310 --> 00:08:55.750
Let's see what you can do!
Take your positions!

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:06.020
Jerid!

00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:07.230
Mouar!

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:09.050
You seem to be having fun at your end.

00:09:09.930 --> 00:09:12.360
<i>Don't let something like this irritate you!</i>

00:09:14.230 --> 00:09:16.560
Also watch out for
the enemy, Lt. Jerid.

00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:17.730
<i>Roger.</i>

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:20.840
So, he'll be looking after those two.

00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:25.130
He's not what I imagined
from what Jamaican told me.

00:09:33.350 --> 00:09:34.150
Taking off.

00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:51.060
Show me your so-called "qualities"!

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:54.070
Looks like he's serious.

00:09:55.070 --> 00:09:56.200
Listen!

00:09:56.270 --> 00:09:58.210
Our enemy is the Argama
and the Argama alone!

00:09:58.280 --> 00:09:59.440
We have no other!

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:03.310
I hate to correct you, but our enemy
is all of the A.E.U.G.!

00:10:03.380 --> 00:10:06.370
I'm telling you that the A.E.U.G. hinges
on the Argama plus the Gundam Mk. II...

00:10:06.450 --> 00:10:08.250
...and the new model mobile suit.

00:10:08.890 --> 00:10:11.190
Keep quiet when you don't know
what you're doing!

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:13.650
How can he be so sure of that?

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:18.190
<i>I remember hearing about a pilot</i>
<i>with battle experience, Lila, I think...</i>

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:20.460
<i>...who lost to the will-power</i>
<i>of the Argama.</i>

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:22.160
<i>Chief Petty Officer Sarah, let's go!</i>

00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:31.640
Is it the Argama?

00:10:32.580 --> 00:10:34.170
It's fast.

00:10:35.380 --> 00:10:36.570
Wh-What?!

00:10:39.880 --> 00:10:40.850
Wh-What's that?!

00:10:49.190 --> 00:10:50.890
I don't believe that's one of the Titans'.

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:53.820
Is it a new A.E.U.G. mobile armor?

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:02.000
There are no other machines nearby.

00:11:02.070 --> 00:11:04.470
Siddeley, try making contact with it!

00:11:04.740 --> 00:11:07.110
That'll determine whether
it's an enemy or ally.

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:08.370
<i>Right.</i>

00:11:11.180 --> 00:11:12.510
That's... a Marasai?

00:11:12.580 --> 00:11:13.980
Titans!

00:11:14.050 --> 00:11:15.380
A hell of a place to be found by them!

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:21.430
Which means the Argama
shouldn't be too far away.

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:23.120
<i>I'm going to contact the Dogosse Gier!</i>

00:11:23.190 --> 00:11:24.530
No, we don't have time for that!

00:11:24.730 --> 00:11:26.060
We'll continue on and
lure the Argama out!

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:29.100
But we don't know where the Argama is.

00:11:29.170 --> 00:11:31.000
- <i>Just do as I say!</i>
- <i>Roger!</i>

00:11:31.070 --> 00:11:32.370
Siddeley! You're being careless!

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:35.900
Chief Petty Officer Sarah, what's the
big idea interfering with my orders?!

00:11:36.910 --> 00:11:38.900
<i>Lieutenant Jerid's being hasty.</i>

00:11:38.980 --> 00:11:39.940
Roger!

00:11:41.910 --> 00:11:43.740
That's the right answer.

00:11:51.260 --> 00:11:52.590
Are you okay with this?

00:11:52.660 --> 00:11:56.250
I believe I can trust the Lieutenant
and his straightforwardness!

00:11:56.330 --> 00:11:57.120
However...!

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:14.210
The Defenser's been found by the enemy?!

00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:15.750
Beam flashes confirmed
from two o'clock.

00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:18.580
- Back them up!
- Y-Yes, sir!

00:12:20.120 --> 00:12:22.380
All units, take battle positions!
Locate the enemies!

00:12:24.290 --> 00:12:25.150
You're fast.

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:26.820
Ensign Reccoa's coming, right?

00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:27.690
Ensign Reccoa is?

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:29.650
Yes, she should be coming.

00:12:29.730 --> 00:12:31.700
Kamille, sorry about what I said earlier.

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:33.060
Roger!

00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:34.960
<i>What was that?</i>

00:12:35.030 --> 00:12:37.760
<i>I said it so he wouldn't be bothered by it</i>
<i>in battle!</i>

00:12:48.110 --> 00:12:49.550
- I'm taking the Zeta Gundam out!
- <i>Roger.</i>

00:12:54.690 --> 00:12:56.050
Kamille, let's do it!

00:12:59.720 --> 00:13:00.660
Is it ready?!

00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:02.780
Go ahead! The lever's been adjusted
for you, Lieutenant!

00:13:02.860 --> 00:13:03.690
Thank you!

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:04.890
The Mk. II's going!

00:13:05.460 --> 00:13:06.790
Where's my mobile suit?!

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:09.460
We're not bringing out the Nemos yet!
It's too far away!

00:13:10.770 --> 00:13:12.290
What about this Rick Dias?!

00:13:12.370 --> 00:13:13.530
Lieutenant Batch will be using that!

00:13:13.610 --> 00:13:15.040
I see.

00:13:16.410 --> 00:13:18.270
Emma! Gundam Mk. II! Taking off!

00:13:23.620 --> 00:13:25.640
What's going on?! Fa's taking off?!

00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:28.020
- Is she experienced?!
- She's on "Actual Battle Version 1B".

00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:29.710
Where's Apolly?!

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:32.150
<i>Apolly's Rick Dias has just mounted</i>
<i>the catapult!</i>

00:13:33.020 --> 00:13:33.750
Apolly!

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:35.820
Fa's taking off in a Rick Dias!
Look after her!

00:13:36.360 --> 00:13:37.290
Why should I?

00:13:37.360 --> 00:13:38.990
- <i>Just go!</i>
- Roger!

00:13:39.330 --> 00:13:42.860
Damn! Do I need to have high hopes
for Newtypes?

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:45.170
Is that why Fa was assigned here?

00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:48.200
Fa Yuiry! Rick Dias! Taking off!

00:13:52.210 --> 00:13:54.410
Jerid's unit has come across the enemy?

00:13:54.610 --> 00:13:55.640
It appears that way.

00:13:55.710 --> 00:13:58.510
This once again shows
how very lucky Jerid is.

00:13:58.620 --> 00:14:00.710
Other crafts are approaching
at a great speed!

00:14:00.990 --> 00:14:02.080
That must be the Argama unit.

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:03.380
- I'm going, too.
- Wait!

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:05.760
Care to join me and watch...

00:14:06.060 --> 00:14:08.490
...to see how well Lieutenant Jerid
can handle the situation?

00:14:08.560 --> 00:14:09.990
That might not be bad thing.

00:14:10.060 --> 00:14:14.230
If you want to see those young pilots you
recommended crush the Argama, that is.

00:14:14.300 --> 00:14:14.860
However...!

00:14:14.930 --> 00:14:18.030
I never gave Jerid's unit permission to fight!

00:14:18.340 --> 00:14:20.300
Therefore, seeing that he's started it...

00:14:20.370 --> 00:14:23.530
...he must have the confidence
to win this battle alone, right?

00:14:26.580 --> 00:14:31.380
That's why Jerid jumped into this battle
without contacting me.

00:14:31.520 --> 00:14:33.070
So, I won't send out any help.

00:14:43.700 --> 00:14:44.720
Two units.

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:53.230
Match your timing!

00:14:53.300 --> 00:14:54.460
Hide yourself behind your partner!

00:14:54.540 --> 00:14:57.240
But that mobile suit is very quick!

00:14:57.640 --> 00:14:59.470
Two units can't look like one
in space!

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:00.840
Try it before drawing conclusions!

00:15:05.720 --> 00:15:07.120
I'm not letting it get away!

00:15:12.920 --> 00:15:15.980
<i>Ensign, I'll attract the enemy's attention!</i>
<i>Please get the Methuss back to the Argama!</i>

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:17.550
I can't allow that!

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:28.540
I-I got it!

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:38.880
Reinforcements?!

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:42.780
An ally?

00:15:43.490 --> 00:15:44.610
Is it the Gundam Mk. II?!

00:15:52.200 --> 00:15:53.750
The new model. Where's it coming from?

00:15:56.130 --> 00:15:58.500
Siddeley, Sarah! After the two units
that got away!

00:15:58.570 --> 00:15:59.540
<i>Roger!</i>

00:16:02.070 --> 00:16:04.200
Just because you have
one or two extra units helping out...!

00:16:07.710 --> 00:16:08.770
Reinforcements?!

00:16:08.850 --> 00:16:10.470
Three of them!

00:16:15.090 --> 00:16:18.320
Is it because we failed to hide each other
like Lieutenant Jerid ordered us to?!

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:28.830
You!

00:16:28.900 --> 00:16:30.870
You must act on Apolly's orders!

00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:32.290
I know that.

00:16:33.540 --> 00:16:34.510
Fa!

00:16:39.340 --> 00:16:40.570
Ensign Reccoa?

00:16:40.650 --> 00:16:42.310
Lieutenant Emma?!

00:16:42.380 --> 00:16:44.370
- Any damage?
- I'm all right!

00:16:50.490 --> 00:16:51.960
Gotcha!

00:17:03.600 --> 00:17:04.570
<i>Kamille?!</i>

00:17:07.810 --> 00:17:08.740
Damn!

00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:31.560
I'm out of bullets!

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:35.260
If you didn't come out,
you wouldn't have to die!

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:42.910
- Just leave things to me!
- I was backing you up!

00:17:42.970 --> 00:17:44.460
Fa, what are you doing here?!

00:17:48.010 --> 00:17:50.240
Kamille, we're in the midst of a battle!

00:17:55.620 --> 00:17:56.380
Watch out!

00:17:56.890 --> 00:17:58.250
However!

00:18:06.700 --> 00:18:07.560
Jerid?

00:18:07.630 --> 00:18:09.690
No, I believe Siddeley's been defeated.

00:18:10.370 --> 00:18:12.060
Jerid.

00:18:12.140 --> 00:18:14.470
Unless you destroy two of them,
it won't balance out.

00:18:17.610 --> 00:18:19.440
But he's awfully outnumbered.

00:18:21.610 --> 00:18:23.550
He's returning with his tail
between his legs.

00:18:33.460 --> 00:18:34.620
I'm going to get killed.

00:18:34.690 --> 00:18:36.660
The minds of the enemies
are becoming one...

00:18:37.030 --> 00:18:37.930
...and coming at me!

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:46.070
Sarah, don't retreat without my orders!

00:18:56.950 --> 00:18:59.750
Kamille! He's saved by the strengths
of that new model.

00:19:10.530 --> 00:19:12.520
Laugh at me if you wish.

00:19:12.600 --> 00:19:14.190
I've lost Siddeley.

00:19:14.570 --> 00:19:16.660
Being able to escape
is a victory in itself.

00:19:17.270 --> 00:19:19.860
Are you mocking me since I've already
lost one of my people?

00:19:19.940 --> 00:19:20.930
Not at all!

00:19:21.010 --> 00:19:23.130
Yes, what Mouar says is correct.

00:19:27.110 --> 00:19:28.440
You did fine.

00:19:28.510 --> 00:19:31.680
Thanks to you, we had a chance
to observe the enemy's mobile suit.

00:19:32.550 --> 00:19:35.610
If we look at it as a plan to
gather information, it was a success.

00:19:36.490 --> 00:19:38.080
I'm very sorry.

00:19:38.160 --> 00:19:39.880
I lost an important pilot.

00:19:41.160 --> 00:19:44.690
Aren't you going to ask me why
I didn't send out reinforcements?

00:19:45.300 --> 00:19:48.030
Our immediate objective lies with
Operation Apollo.

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:51.130
We haven't got the time
to be dealing with the Argama.

00:19:54.570 --> 00:19:56.900
Do you really believe that's the reason?

00:19:56.970 --> 00:19:57.910
Yes, sir.

00:19:57.980 --> 00:19:59.170
Okay. Get some rest.

00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:03.570
- Sarah, stay here.
- Yes?

00:20:04.920 --> 00:20:07.650
I understand you retreated
before your squadron leader.

00:20:10.490 --> 00:20:12.960
I could see the minds of many enemies.

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:14.290
I've never faced such a situation.

00:20:14.360 --> 00:20:15.330
Hmm.

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:18.620
Therefore... I was scared.

00:20:19.360 --> 00:20:21.230
Will you get used to it?

00:20:21.670 --> 00:20:23.760
If those are your orders,
I will get used to it.

00:20:23.830 --> 00:20:25.170
I'll try.

00:20:25.370 --> 00:20:27.670
Okay. That's all I wanted to hear.

00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:30.900
Sarah, you can do it.

00:20:32.180 --> 00:20:34.300
I look forward to it.

00:20:34.380 --> 00:20:35.680
Yes, sir.

00:20:43.790 --> 00:20:46.090
The G-Defenser has arrived safely.
Good work.

00:20:47.490 --> 00:20:49.760
I got the Methuss damaged
right from the start.

00:20:50.430 --> 00:20:52.730
Make your apologies to the mechanics.

00:20:52.800 --> 00:20:57.060
We have some parts, and we should be
okay once we meet up with the Radish.

00:20:57.130 --> 00:20:57.930
Right.

00:20:59.670 --> 00:21:01.400
I can't allow someone like you...

00:21:01.470 --> 00:21:03.440
...to get emotional and disrupt
our battle strategy!

00:21:03.540 --> 00:21:04.770
I'm very sorry!

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:08.940
But I couldn't stay back and not fight!

00:21:09.150 --> 00:21:11.080
You haven't even had sufficient training!

00:21:11.150 --> 00:21:13.140
I had gone as far as the
"Actual Battle Version"!

00:21:13.220 --> 00:21:15.450
Training and actual battle are worlds apart!

00:21:15.520 --> 00:21:17.490
- In addition...
- <i>It's my fault.</i>

00:21:17.560 --> 00:21:20.320
<i>I'm the one who made Fa so frustrated.</i>

00:21:21.060 --> 00:21:24.320
Lieutenant, I'm also to blame
for Fa's actions.

00:21:24.400 --> 00:21:26.020
Apolly, I apologize.

00:21:26.100 --> 00:21:27.590
- S-Sure.
- Captain Bright!

00:21:27.670 --> 00:21:29.790
I gave her permission to sortie.

00:21:30.770 --> 00:21:34.760
However, Fa, what you did this time
was not good. Just understand that.

00:21:35.470 --> 00:21:36.530
I understand!

00:21:36.610 --> 00:21:38.580
But humans are animals
that act on emotion.

00:21:40.540 --> 00:21:44.840
At war, you can't sink a battleship
with your temporary emotions alone!

00:21:45.950 --> 00:21:46.920
Y-Yes.

00:21:48.520 --> 00:21:50.820
You're... right.

00:21:52.590 --> 00:21:54.080
Long time no see.

00:21:54.160 --> 00:21:56.130
I'm pleased to see that you're well.

00:21:56.190 --> 00:21:58.060
It's good to be young, isn't it?

00:21:58.130 --> 00:21:59.460
Do you think so?

00:21:59.530 --> 00:22:01.000
I don't quite understand.

00:22:01.670 --> 00:22:03.830
You're going to miss being
scolded like that.

00:22:03.900 --> 00:22:04.490
Okay, Fa.

00:22:04.570 --> 00:22:07.560
- Get some rest!
- Yes, sir! I'll be excused!

00:22:07.640 --> 00:22:08.800
See ya.

00:22:08.870 --> 00:22:10.600
Go and comfort Fa.

00:22:10.680 --> 00:22:11.470
I know.

00:22:11.710 --> 00:22:12.610
Ensign.

00:22:12.680 --> 00:22:14.170
This is from Commander Henken.

00:22:15.880 --> 00:22:17.180
Thank you.

00:22:18.880 --> 00:22:20.820
But... I'm at a loss...!

00:22:20.890 --> 00:22:22.280
What shall I do with this?

00:22:22.350 --> 00:22:24.820
Don't ask me. It's not a present to me.

00:22:25.160 --> 00:22:27.720
Well, I've handed it to you,
haven't I, Emma?

00:22:28.290 --> 00:22:29.260
Reccoa...!

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.600
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:45.980 --> 00:23:49.940
The fleet led by Scirocco
attacks Von Braun City.

00:23:50.580 --> 00:23:54.350
The Dogosse Gier evades
the Argama's defensive line...

00:23:54.420 --> 00:23:56.720
...and makes a forced landing.

00:23:57.290 --> 00:24:01.390
The Argama is silenced by Scirocco's
unexpected, headstrong tactic.

00:24:02.360 --> 00:24:06.890
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam,
"Moon Attack!"

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
Next Episode

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
Moon Attack!

00:24:07.500 --> 00:24:10.500
You will see the tears of time.
